<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec c/a surplus falls 23.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec c/a surplus falls 23.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The surplus in Japan's current account, the broadest measure of trade in goods and services, shrank 23.1 percent to 820.7 billion yen in December from a year earlier, the Finance Ministry announced on Monday.</p>
<p>The surplus in merchandise trade alone also fell 20.0 percent to 1.046 trillion yen from the same month a year earlier.</p>
</text>
